  "name": "Varicella Zoster IgG",
  "code": "VARIG",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p style=\"margin-right:12.0pt;margin-left:2.0pt;text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Varicella-Zoster Virus (VZV) causes chicken pox and when reactivated, potentially decades later, causes shingles. Twenty percent of adults will develop shingles, a rash or blister of the skin that may cause severe pain. Varicella-Zoster IgG, EIA reliably measures immunity due to previous infection but is unsuitable for detection of post-vaccination immune status.</span></p>",
